Let the overlay's //tools/fidlgen_rust alias see fidlgen_rust (milestone M7).

Upstream makes the binary visible only to its FIDL rules (//build/bazel/rules, which
regen.py maps to //vendor/fuchsia/build/bazel/rules). The overlay runs it through
//tools/fidlgen_rust, and M8's rule will use that label. The added line is the overlay's
(Apache-2.0); the context lines are Fuchsia's (BSD-2-Clause, LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause.txt).
Applied by scripts/regen.py to the rewritten BUILD.bazel.

diff --git a/tools/fidl/fidlgen_rust/BUILD.bazel b/tools/fidl/fidlgen_rust/BUILD.bazel
index 6829e66..7f063c4 100644
--- a/tools/fidl/fidlgen_rust/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/tools/fidl/fidlgen_rust/BUILD.bazel
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ go_binary_host_tool(
     srcs = ["main.go"],
     target_compatible_with = HOST_CONSTRAINTS,
     visibility = [
+        "//tools/fidlgen_rust:__pkg__",
         "//vendor/fuchsia/build/bazel/rules:__subpackages__",
     ],
     deps = [
